WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.433 --> 00:00:03.667
AI Restaurant Booker
calls restaurants for you.

2
00:00:03.667 --> 00:00:07.800
Choose your restaurants, set their
priority order, and enter your booking

3
00:00:07.800 --> 00:00:12.467
details. It works through your list
with your date, time, party size,

4
00:00:12.467 --> 00:00:16.267
and requirements, stopping
when a table is confirmed.

5
00:00:20.433 --> 00:00:22.467
Choose Madrid or Navarra.

6
00:00:22.467 --> 00:00:26.800
Find your restaurants, save favorites,
and drag your shortlist into priority

7
00:00:26.800 --> 00:00:31.067
order. Four guests. Nine o’clock.

8
00:00:31.067 --> 00:00:33.467
Thirty minutes of flexibility.

9
00:00:33.467 --> 00:00:38.333
Add seating preferences, dietary
requirements, and a special request.

10
00:00:38.333 --> 00:00:42.833
Start the booking. Voice takes
on the restaurant contact.

11
00:00:42.833 --> 00:00:45.167
The first restaurant is full.

12
00:00:45.167 --> 00:00:49.233
The second proposes ten thirty,
beyond the allowed window.

13
00:00:49.233 --> 00:00:51.233
The workflow moves on.

14
00:00:51.233 --> 00:00:55.967
The third provides confirmation evidence,
and the result appears right here.

15
00:00:55.967 --> 00:00:58.433
Your requirements stay in control.

16
00:01:00.433 --> 00:01:04.600
AI Control Center takes you inside
the work behind each booking.

17
00:01:04.600 --> 00:01:07.833
Open a restaurant contact to see
its result and the AI workflow

18
00:01:07.833 --> 00:01:09.800
recorded for that call.

19
00:01:09.800 --> 00:01:13.733
Compare your three contacts, then
follow the agents from the first action

20
00:01:13.733 --> 00:01:15.567
to the final outcome.

21
00:01:25.433 --> 00:01:29.667
For each call, Control Center shows
how the AI agents worked: which

22
00:01:29.667 --> 00:01:33.100
agent acted, when, and in what order.

23
00:01:33.100 --> 00:01:35.433
The graph connects their actions.

24
00:01:35.433 --> 00:01:40.267
This illustration follows Voice as it
sends a proposed time to Negotiation.

25
00:01:40.267 --> 00:01:44.233
Negotiation checks your limits and
returns a decision so Voice can continue

26
00:01:44.233 --> 00:01:46.600
within the terms you authorized.

27
00:01:46.600 --> 00:01:50.367
Verification then checks the
final confirmation evidence.

28
00:01:50.367 --> 00:01:55.067
Back in the recorded workflow, inspect
each agent’s actions, tools, and saved

29
00:01:55.067 --> 00:01:59.767
results. Memory and Summary
records the outcome; Evaluation

30
00:01:59.767 --> 00:02:04.067
checks consistency. Select an event
and follow the timeline to see the

31
00:02:04.067 --> 00:02:07.667
sequence of agent handoffs and
what happened at each moment.

32
00:02:10.433 --> 00:02:13.967
The second attempt tells us
why the workflow moved on.

33
00:02:13.967 --> 00:02:17.733
We asked for nine; the
restaurant offered ten thirty.

34
00:02:17.733 --> 00:02:20.933
Ninety minutes exceeds the
thirty-minute allowance.

35
00:02:20.933 --> 00:02:25.700
Offer Review exposes the recorded
policy decision: unacceptable.

36
00:02:25.700 --> 00:02:30.100
Beside it, the backend tool shows
how the attempt was processed.

37
00:02:30.100 --> 00:02:34.800
These are the stored events, separate
from the illustrated voice handoff.

38
00:02:34.800 --> 00:02:38.300
The timeline connects each
operation to its duration.

39
00:02:38.300 --> 00:02:41.867
Replay follows that history
without making another call.

40
00:02:41.867 --> 00:02:46.333
And the third attempt closes the loop:
explicit confirmation evidence, checked

41
00:02:46.333 --> 00:02:49.433
against the request and
linked to the final result.

42
00:02:55.433 --> 00:02:59.567
Analytics brings outcomes and timings
together, making patterns easier to

43
00:02:59.567 --> 00:03:04.567
spot. In Playground, run a
scenario, review its checks,

44
00:03:04.567 --> 00:03:07.867
and open the trace—all
inside the demo environment.

45
00:03:08.433 --> 00:03:12.167
AI Restaurant Booker. A simple experience.

46
00:03:12.167 --> 00:03:14.333
An inspectable execution.
